Original commit body from cdb16320d19fc65e188e386a8cbab6bc5e2b3ded:

`git checkout -b feature dev` leaves HEAD at dev's tip. Until the branch
makes a commit of its own, `git commit --amend` rewrites that INHERITED
base commit -- folding staged work into it while keeping its message,
author and author-date -- so the work merges impersonating whatever the
base tip happened to be. auto-pr amends HEAD at three sites and none
checked ownership.

Live instance 2026-07-29: dev's tip was a tracker sync commit, so seven
files of analyzer work landed on dev subjected "tracker: 6 files (104
ops)". The decisive evidence is an absence -- that branch's reflog reads
checkout -> commit (amend) -> checkout, while every healthy branch that
day reads checkout -> commit -> commit (amend) -> checkout.

All three sites now call _assert_branch_owns_head, which refuses when
`git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD <base>` holds. That predicate beats
counting base..HEAD: it asks whether HEAD is already contained in the
base, and stays correct after a rebase onto a moved base. It takes
several candidate refs and fails open when none resolve.

The filing blamed tracker auto-sync and proposed three fixes, all wrong:
the tracker has zero --amend calls (do_sync has used plumbing with no
checkout since 2026-03-06); deferring sync on PR_PENDING is orthogonal
(the sync's ff preceded branch creation by 16s); and capturing the body
early is already the behavior (DESC is read at :1428, the amend is at
:1430) -- the note recorded a bare sign-off because there was never a
good message to read.

Tests extract the guard's real definition from the script rather than
restating it, so they cannot drift from what ships. Includes a positive
control that reproduces the damage from scratch with no tracker involved
-- the only test green before the fix -- and a ratchet that fails if any
`git commit --amend` in the script is left unguarded.

The suite is named tests/test_auto_pr.py because the WI-jozan mapper
selects exactly `tests/test_<script name>.py`; under any other name
nothing selects it and ci.yml skips pytest, so the ratchet would have
been vacuous in CI while passing locally. That the mapper is 1:1 leaves
the ten pre-existing tests/test_autopr_*.py files unselected; filed as
WI-bisar.

